<body>

<div class="stack">
<article class="sheet">
  <span class="staple" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <header class="letterhead">
    <div class="org"><b>North Sound Drilling Ltd.</b><br>Platform Kestrel, Block 14/7, North Atlantic</div>
    <div class="docref">Form HS-14, revision 3<br>Page 1 of 1</div>
  </header>

  <a class="sticky" href="#download">download is in section 5 ↓</a>

  <div class="titleblock">
    <p class="typed-title">Night shift induction, all crew</p>
    <p class="typed-sub">Read before your first shift. Keep this sheet with you.</p>
    <h1>Does anyone copy?</h1>
    <span class="stamp">Night shift<small>no relief until dawn</small></span>
  </div>

  <section class="row">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>1. The posting</h2>
      <p>You are one of a crew of two to eight, on an offshore platform, for five night shifts. Nobody else is out here. The helicopter comes at dawn, but only if the rig is still running and the helipad is lit.</p>
      <p>Two weeks ago the drill went through something on the seabed that wasn't rock. Since then, crews have reported hearing each other on the radio when nobody was transmitting.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="note">it learns your voice</aside>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>2. Radio procedure</h2>
      <p>Your walkie is the only way to reach the rest of the crew. Keep transmissions short. Below is channel 4 from the previous crew's last night.</p>
      <div class="printout" role="figure" aria-label="Radio transcript">
        <div><span class="t">02:11</span>  PELL   Generator's back up. Heading to the pump room.</div>
        <div><span class="t">02:11</span>  MARA   Copy. Jonah, you still with me on the stairs?</div>
        <div><span class="t">02:12</span>  JONAH  Right behind you.</div>
        <div><span class="t">02:12</span>  MARA   Pell, did you just call me?</div>
        <div><span class="t">02:13</span>  PELL   No. I haven't keyed in since the generator.</div>
        <div><span class="circled"><span class="t">02:13</span>  JONAH  Right behind you.<svg viewBox="0 0 300 40" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 22 C 20 6, 120 2, 220 5 S 296 14, 290 24 S 200 38, 120 37 S 6 34, 10 20 S 40 8, 60 7" fill="none" stroke="#a8261d" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/></svg></span></div>
        <div><span class="t">02:13</span>         <span class="static">.. ·.. ··· (static) ·· ..</span></div>
        <div><span class="t">02:14</span>  MARA   Jonah? Does anyone copy?</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="note down">he never said it twice
      <svg viewBox="0 0 70 34" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M64 4 C 50 10, 30 22, 6 26 M6 26 L 16 18 M6 26 L 17 32" fill="none" stroke="#a8261d" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>3. Duties each shift</h2>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 14 L 10 21 L 24 2" fill="none" stroke="#a8261d" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Keep the generators fuelled.</li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 13 L 11 20 L 23 4" fill="none" stroke="#a8261d" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Restart the pumps when the lower decks flood.</li>
        <li>Keep the comms mast up.</li>
        <li>Light the helipad before dawn.</li>
        <li>Stay with your crew.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The work is spread over the whole rig, so you'll have to split up. If someone falls behind, go back for them. If two of them come back, use a flare.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="note down">and count them. every time.</aside>
  </section>

  <section class="row" id="photos">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>4. Photographs</h2>
      <p>From the crew Polaroid. It's the only thing on board that sometimes catches what the rest of us can't see. Nobody remembers taking the last one.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="note">look at the third one</aside>
      <div class="photos" id="photo-wall">
        <figure class="polaroid"><div class="frame blank-1"></div><figcaption>deck B, 02:40</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="polaroid"><div class="frame blank-2"></div><figcaption>pump room</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="polaroid"><div class="frame blank-3"></div><figcaption>who is that?</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" id="download">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>5. Equipment issue</h2>
      <div class="form">
        <div class="f"><div class="k">Item</div><div class="v">Does Anyone Copy? (game)</div></div>
        <div class="f"><div class="k">Revision</div><div class="v" id="f-version">checking…</div></div>
        <div class="f"><div class="k">Issued</div><div class="v" id="f-date">–</div></div>
        <div class="f"><div class="k">Size</div><div class="v" id="f-size">–</div></div>
        <div class="f"><div class="k">For</div><div class="v">Windows 10 / 11, 64-bit</div></div>
      </div>
      <a class="dl" id="dl" href="#download" aria-disabled="true">Checking for the latest build…</a>
      <a class="older" id="older" href="#" hidden>older revisions</a>

      <div class="amend">
        <h3>Changes since the last revision</h3>
        <div id="notes"><p>Listed here with each new build.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:22px">To install</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Unzip the download anywhere.</li>
        <li>Run the .exe inside the folder.</li>
        <li>If Windows SmartScreen stops it, choose More info, then Run anyway.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <aside class="note down" id="dl-note">take the newest one</aside>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <div class="body">
      <h2>6. Before you sign</h2>
      <p>You will need at least one other crew member, a microphone and headphones. Voice chat is recorded for the length of the shift so it can be played back. Recordings are not kept after the shift ends.</p>
      <p>By signing below you confirm you have read this sheet.</p>
      <div class="sigs">
        <div class="sig"><span>Mara Okafor</span><small>Crew member</small></div>
        <div class="sig"><span>D. Pell</span><small>Crew member</small></div>
        <div class="sig"><span>Jonah Reyes</span><small>Crew member</small></div>
        <div class="sig"><span>Jonah Reyes</span><small>Crew member</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="note down sig-note">there were only three of us</aside>
  </section>

  <footer class="foot">
    <span>Does Anyone Copy? is still in development. Some things will break.</span>
    <span>HS-14 / rev. 3</span>
  </footer>
</article>
</div>

<script>
(() => {
  const cfg = window.DAC_CONFIG || {};
  function findRepo() {
    if (cfg.owner && cfg.repo) return { owner: cfg.owner, repo: cfg.repo };
    const host = location.hostname;
    if (host.endsWith(".github.io")) {
      const owner = host.split(".")[0];
      const first = location.pathname.split("/").filter(Boolean)[0];
      return { owner, repo: first || `${owner}.github.io` };
    }
    return null;
  }
  const esc = s => String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;", "'": "&#39;" }[c]));
  const size = b => b >= 1e9 ? (b / 1e9).toFixed(2) + " GB" : Math.max(1, Math.round(b / 1e6)) + " MB";
  const date = s => new Date(s).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" });

  function renderNotes(md) {
    if (!md || !md.trim()) return "<p>No changes listed for this revision.</p>";
    const inline = s => esc(s).replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, "<strong>$1</strong>").replace(/`(.+?)`/g, "<code>$1</code>");
    let html = "", list = false;
    for (const raw of md.replace(/\r/g, "").split("\n")) {
      const line = raw.trim();
      const item = line.match(/^[-*]\s+(.*)/);
      if (item) { if (!list) { html += "<ul>"; list = true; } html += `<li>${inline(item[1])}</li>`; continue; }
      if (list) { html += "</ul>"; list = false; }
      if (!line) continue;
      const head = line.match(/^#{1,6}\s+(.*)/);
      html += head ? `<h4>${inline(head[1])}</h4>` : `<p>${inline(line)}</p>`;
    }
    if (list) html += "</ul>";
    return html;
  }
  function pickAsset(assets) {
    if (!assets || !assets.length) return null;
    if (cfg.preferredAsset) {
      const hit = assets.find(a => a.name.toLowerCase().includes(cfg.preferredAsset.toLowerCase()));
      if (hit) return hit;
    }
    const builds = assets.filter(a => /\.(zip|7z|rar|exe|msi)$/i.test(a.name));
    return (builds.length ? builds : assets).sort((a, b) => b.size - a.size)[0];
  }

  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
  function setButton(href, label, enabled) {
    const b = $("dl");
    b.href = href; b.textContent = label;
    b.setAttribute("aria-disabled", enabled ? "false" : "true");
  }

  async function loadBuild() {
    const repo = findRepo();
    if (!repo) {
      $("f-version").textContent = "not issued yet";
      setButton("#download", "Not available yet", false);
      $("dl-note").textContent = "set the repo in DAC_CONFIG (top of index.html)";
      return;
    }
    const releases = `https://github.com/${repo.owner}/${repo.repo}/releases`;
    $("older").href = releases; $("older").hidden = false;
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`https://api.github.com/repos/${repo.owner}/${repo.repo}/releases/latest`, { headers: { Accept: "application/vnd.github+json" } });
      if (res.status === 404) throw new Error("none");
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error("http " + res.status);
      const rel = await res.json();
      const asset = pickAsset(rel.assets);
      const version = rel.tag_name || rel.name || "latest";
      $("f-version").textContent = version;
      $("f-date").textContent = date(rel.published_at);
      if (asset) {
        $("f-size").textContent = size(asset.size);
        setButton(asset.browser_download_url, `Download ${version} for Windows`, true);
      } else {
        setButton(rel.html_url, "Open the download page", true);
      }
      $("notes").innerHTML = renderNotes(rel.body);
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.message === "none") {
        $("f-version").textContent = "not issued yet";
        setButton(releases, "See releases", true);
      } else {
        $("f-version").textContent = "see releases";
        setButton(`${releases}/latest`, "Open the latest release", true);
      }
    }
  }
  loadBuild();

  /* screenshots/1.jpg … 8.jpg replace the blank Polaroids */
  const captions = ["deck B, 02:40", "pump room", "who is that?", "night 2", "the stairs", "helipad", "don't remember this", "?"];
  const wall = $("photo-wall");
  const found = [];
  let pending = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= 8; i++) {
    let tried = 0;
    for (const ext of ["jpg", "png"]) {
      pending++;
      const img = new Image();
      img.onload = () => { if (!found.some(f => f.n === i)) found.push({ n: i, src: img.src }); done(); };
      img.onerror = done;
      img.src = `screenshots/${i}.${ext}`;
    }
  }
  function done() {
    if (--pending > 0 || !found.length) return;
    found.sort((a, b) => a.n - b.n);
    wall.innerHTML = found.slice(0, 5).map(f =>
      `<figure class="polaroid"><div class="frame"><img src="${esc(f.src)}" alt="Screenshot ${f.n}" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>${esc(captions[f.n - 1])}</figcaption></figure>`
    ).join("");
  }
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
